MAME Attribution
================

This emulator's design is informed by the MAME nakajies driver and
associated device emulations, all BSD-3-Clause licensed.  No MAME source
code was copied; the implementation is original.

MAME copyright holders whose work informed this project:

  Wilbert Pol, Sandro Ronco   - nakajies driver (ES-2xx typewriter family)
  Bryan McPhail               - NEC V20/V30 CPU core and cycle timing
  smf, Robbbert               - i8251 USART
  Curt Coder                  - RP5C01 RTC
  smf, hap                    - clock device
  Kevin Thacker               - beeper sound device
  Dirk Best                   - PC Card SRAM
  smf                         - PC Card slot interface (GPL-2.0+; see note)

Note on pccard.h (GPL-2.0+)
----------------------------
The MAME PC Card slot interface header (bus/pccard/pccard.h) is licensed
GPL-2.0+, unlike the rest of the referenced MAME sources.  Our PC Card
implementation does not derive from that code; it is a trivial SRAM buffer
with file-backed persistence, implementing the hardware banking spec
directly.  The GPL-licensed header was read for reference only.
